From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Caner Altinbasak <cal@brightsign.biz>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 13:42:56 +0100
Subject: fix: run video teardown on compositor thread OS-22333

WebMediaPlayerBrightsign::Shutdown() called SetVideoFrameProviderClient(
nullptr) on the main render thread, which reaches into cc::
VideoFrameProviderClientImpl::StopUsingProvider() -> StopRendering() ->
RemoveVideoFrameController(). That call chain assumes the compositor/impl
task runner, but the assumption is only enforced by a DCHECK, which is
compiled out in release builds.

Under hwz:off create/destroy churn this let Shutdown() force a compositor
draw from the wrong thread, crashing in Viz's mojo IPC
(CHECK(sequence_checker_.CalledOnValidSequence()) in
mojo::InterfaceEndpointClient::SendMessage). Confirmed on both Nexus and
Rockchip crash dumps captured from tests/html/21701 and tests/html/21695,
so this is a shared-code race rather than a native-backend bug.

Hop the StopUsingProvider() call to compositor_task_runner_ and block on
a WaitableEvent until it completes, instead of calling it inline on
main_task_runner_. This still runs synchronously before vid_player_ and
the shared-memory frame cache are torn down below (as the prior code
required), but now on the thread cc actually expects; it also leaves the
client's internal |provider_| pointer null, so a later cc-driven
VideoLayerImpl teardown safely no-ops instead of touching a
possibly-destroyed WebMediaPlayerBrightsign.

diff --git a/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/media/brightsign/web_media_player_brightsign.cc b/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/media/brightsign/web_media_player_brightsign.cc
index 445c9dd7741f81f33b1aab86194c05e4338677de..b4144ed8423495e6a8512b729aa320f2975718fd 100644
--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/media/brightsign/web_media_player_brightsign.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/media/brightsign/web_media_player_brightsign.cc
@@ -8,6 +8,7 @@
 #include "base/command_line.h"
 #include "base/task/bind_post_task.h"
 #include "base/task/thread_pool.h"
+#include "base/synchronization/waitable_event.h"
 #include "base/time/time.h"
 #include "cc/layers/video_layer.h"
 #include "media/base/media_track.h"
@@ -255,8 +256,21 @@ void WebMediaPlayerBrightsign::Shutdown() {
   weak_factory_.InvalidateWeakPtrs();
 
   // Detach the compositor and drop the retained frame before releasing the
-  // shared-memory cache.
-  SetVideoFrameProviderClient(nullptr);
+  // shared-memory cache. StopUsingProvider() must run on the compositor task
+  // runner (cc assumes this, only via a release-stripped DCHECK), so hop
+  // there and block rather than calling it inline on main_task_runner_. The
+  // client is only touched inside that task: cc frees it on the same thread.
+  base::WaitableEvent done;
+  if (compositor_task_runner_->PostTask(
+          FROM_HERE,
+          base::BindOnce(
+              [](WebMediaPlayerBrightsign* player, base::WaitableEvent* done) {
+                player->SetVideoFrameProviderClient(nullptr);
+                done->Signal();
+              },
+              base::Unretained(this), &done))) {
+    done.Wait();
+  }
   {
     base::AutoLock auto_lock(current_frame_lock_);
     current_frame_ = nullptr;
